{% import "macros/datatable.njk" as dt %}
<h1>Tapestries</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Purely decorative placed blocks with no recipe or drop table, so they don't appear anywhere else
  on this wiki &mdash; see the <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}info/">Info</a> page for why.
  {{ generated.tapestries.length }} catalogued directly from the game's block definitions.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  Tapestries have no fixed text of their own &mdash; a placed tapestry shows one chapter of the
  "Tapestry" lore book, picked at placement time, not encoded in its block code. This wiki doesn't
  yet resolve which specific chapter any one placed tapestry shows; each entry below links to the
  book instead. Further parsing of placement-time state would be needed to determine a tapestry's
  true individual name/content.
</p>
<p class="muted">Source: <code>blocktypes/cloth/tapestry.json</code>.</p>

{% call dt.datatable(60, "Search tapestries...", ["Name", "Mod"]) %}
{% for item in generated.tapestries | sort(false, false, "displayName") %}
  <tr data-search="{{ item.domain }}:{{ item.code }}" data-mod="{{ item.sourceMod }}">
    <td><a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tapestries/{{ item.domain }}/{{ item.code | slugify }}/">{{ item.displayName }}</a></td>
    <td><span class="tag">{{ item.sourceMod }}</span></td>
  </tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endcall %}
